From: Nura rc4 <local>
Subject: [PATCH] main: start sensors that were claimed during startup

iio-sensor-proxy owns its bus name before it opens the sensors.  The SSC
drivers' open (ssc_sensor_*_new_sync()) iterates the default main context
while it waits on the DSP, so a Claim*() that arrives right after the name
appears is handled from inside name_acquired_handler().  KWin claims the
accelerometer as soon as the name shows up, so this happens on every start
under Plasma.

That claim either finds no driver yet, or a driver without an open device,
and returns without starting the sensor.  The client stays registered, so
every later Claim*() sees an already-claimed sensor and returns at once
too.  Nothing ever calls set_polling(TRUE): no "Enabling sensor", no
readings, AccelerometerOrientation stays "undefined" and auto-rotation does
nothing.

Treat a driver whose device is not open yet as absent in the claim
handler (it used to call driver_set_polling(NULL) and push to a not yet
allocated invocation array), and at the end of the startup start every
sensor that already has clients, the way the hotplug path in
sensor_changes() does.

---
diff --git a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -522,7 +522,13 @@
 							   NULL);
 		g_hash_table_insert (ht, g_strdup (sender), GUINT_TO_POINTER (watch_id));
 
-		if (driver_type_exists (data, driver_type)) {
+		/* The driver can exist before its device is open: drivers whose
+		 * open waits on the main loop (SSC) let this method call run
+		 * from inside the startup in name_acquired_handler().  Treat
+		 * such a sensor as not there yet; the startup starts it for the
+		 * clients registered here once it is open. */
+		if (driver_type_exists (data, driver_type) &&
+		    DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(driver_type) != NULL) {
 			SensorDevice *sensor_device = DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(driver_type);
 
 			/* No other clients for this sensor? Start it */
@@ -784,6 +790,21 @@
 	if (!any_sensors_left (data))
 		goto bail;
 
+	/* Clients that claimed a sensor while the sensors were being opened
+	 * (KWin claims the accelerometer as soon as the bus name appears) are
+	 * registered but nothing started the sensor for them.  Start it now,
+	 * like the hotplug path does for a sensor that is already claimed. */
+	for (i = 0; i < NUM_SENSOR_TYPES; i++) {
+		if (!driver_type_exists (data, i) ||
+		    g_hash_table_size (data->clients[i]) == 0)
+			continue;
+
+		g_debug ("Starting %s, claimed while the sensors were being opened",
+			 driver_type_to_str (i));
+		data->sensor_startup_dbus_event_delayed[i] = TRUE;
+		driver_set_polling (DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(i), TRUE);
+	}
+
 	send_dbus_event (data, PROP_ALL);
 	send_dbus_event (data, PROP_ALL_COMPASS);
 	return;
